  "words": "The Odyssey is one of the oldest stories ever told, nearly 3,000 years old. But the entire 10-year nightmare happened because one man couldn't keep his mouth shut after winning a fight. Yeah, seriously. Odysseus had already escaped. He was safely sailing away when he turned around and shouted his real name at the monster he'd just blinded. That single moment of ego turned what should have been a 2-week voyage into 10 years of monsters, shipwrecks, angry gods, and disaster."
